  "notes": "A compound verb formed from {拭|ふ}く (to wipe) + {取|と}る (to take/remove). Unlike {拭|ふ}く alone, which simply means to wipe a surface, {拭|ふ}き{取|と}る emphasizes removing something by wiping.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pattern: [object]を{拭|ふ}き{取|と}る\n- No intransitive counterpart\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {汗|あせ}を{拭|ふ}き{取|と}る: to wipe off sweat\n- {涙|なみだ}を{拭|ふ}き{取|と}る: to wipe away tears\n- {汚|よご}れを{拭|ふ}き{取|と}る: to wipe off dirt\n- {水気|みずけ}を{拭|ふ}き{取|と}る: to wipe off moisture\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{拭|ふ}き{取|と}っている describes the action in progress (someone is wiping something off).",
